title: '[pallet-revive] Add debug cargo feature flag'
doc:
- audience: Runtime Dev
  description: |-
    ## Description

      `debug_trace*` RPCs only work when pallet-revive's `DebugEnabled` config is set to `true`.
    Currently only the dev-node has this enabled, but the dev-node is a simplified environment that doesn't fully replicate parachain runtime behavior (e.g. no PoV deduplication).
    To get accurate debug tracing data, it needs to run on parachain runtimes.

    Previously this required editing each runtime's source code to flip `ConstBool<false>` to `ConstBool<true>`.
    This PR adds a `debug` cargo feature flag so debug mode can be toggled at build time without code changes:

      ```bash
      cargo build -p asset-hub-westend-runtime --features debug
      cargo build -p penpal-runtime --features debug
      cargo build -p kitchensink-runtime --features debug
      ```
    ## Integration

      Downstream runtimes using pallet-revive that want this capability need two changes:

      1. Add the feature to Cargo.toml:
    ```diff
    + debug = ["pallet-revive/debug"]
    ```

      2. Switch the config in lib.rs:
      ```diff
    - type DebugEnabled = ConstBool<false>;
    + type DebugEnabled = pallet_revive::DebugIsEnabled;
    ```

      Without these changes, behavior is unchanged (`DebugEnabled` defaults to false).

    ## Review Notes

      - pallet-revive/Cargo.toml: adds empty `debug = []` feature
      - pallet-revive/src/lib.rs: adds `pub type DebugIsEnabled = ConstBool<{ cfg!(feature = "debug") }>`
      - umbrella/Cargo.toml: forwards debug to `pallet-revive?/debug`
      - Runtimes (asset-hub-westend, penpal, kitchensink): add debug feature and switch `DebugEnabled` to `DebugIsEnabled`
      - Dev-node is left as `ConstBool<true>`
crates:
- name: bp-runtime
  bump: patch
- name: asset-hub-westend-runtime
  bump: patch
- name: penpal-runtime
  bump: patch
- name: pallet-revive
  bump: patch
- name: polkadot-sdk
  bump: patch
